    "Registering twice with different emails — duplicates get rejected outright.",
]))
S += chapter(21, "Registration: The 2026 Template", c19)

# ============================================================== CH 20
c20 = []
c20.append(P("180 questions, 180 minutes, one mark a minute before overheads. The "
            "candidates who finish comfortably are not faster readers — they "
            "entered with a plan and refused to improvise mid-paper.", lead))
c20.append(P("A time plan that works", h2))
c20.append(mk_table(
    ["Block", "Minutes", "Job"],
    [["First pass — Biology", "50 - 55", "All 90 questions: answer, shade in batches of 10, flag doubts"],
     ["Second pass — Chemistry", "45 - 50", "All 45: one-step-first policy, park the long numericals"],
     ["Third pass — Physics", "40 - 45", "Easy and medium first; park multi-step numericals"],
     ["Final sweep", "25 - 35", "Parked questions: attempt if you can eliminate two options; verify OMR completeness"]],
    [0.28, 0.16, 0.56]))
c20.append(P("Biology first is deliberate: it is your fastest, highest-yield section, "
            "and banking 300+ marks in the first hour settles nerves for the two "
            "sections that follow. Adjust the order if you are genuinely stronger "
            "elsewhere — but fix the order by February, in mocks, and never change "
            "it on exam day."))
c20.append(P("The negative-marking arithmetic", h2))
c20.append(P("Each question is worth +4 for a right answer and -1 for a wrong one, so "
            "a pure guess (one option in four) has an expected value of zero — 0.25 "
            "chance of +4 equals 0.75 chance of -1. Guessing is therefore only "
            "worthwhile when you can eliminate at least one option: eliminate one "
            "and the expected value turns positive (+0.25); eliminate two and it "
            "jumps to +1. That single habit — never guess on four options, always "
            "guess on two — is worth real marks across a 180-question paper."))
c20.append(bullets([
    "Shade the OMR in batches and check the question-number alignment every batch — one misalignment can ruin a whole row.",
    "Do not leave the OMR for the final ten minutes of the paper; the sweep is for decisions, not for shading.",
    "Use only the pen permitted by the centre's instructions; carry the prescribed ID in original plus photocopy.",
    "Reach the centre well before the reporting time on the admit card; late entry rules are strict and unappealable.",
]))
S += chapter(22, "Exam Day: 180 Minutes, Executed", c20)

# ============================================================== CH 21
c21 = []
c21.append(P("The exam ends, and a second, shorter project begins: converting a "
            "score into a seat. Most aspirants lose seats here not to merit but to "
            "missed deadlines and misunderstood rules.", lead))
c21.append(numbered([
    "Provisional answer keys and your recorded responses are displayed on the NTA site; challenge the questions you can defend within the given window (a fee applies, refunded if your challenge is upheld).",
    "The result arrives as a scorecard with marks and an All India Rank. Category ranks matter as much as the overall rank.",
    "If you are AIQ-eligible, register on the MCC portal (mcc.nic.in), pay the counselling fee and security deposit, and fill choices in order of genuine preference — the order is the whole game.",
    "Register on your state counselling portal in parallel, with your domicile documents ready; for most candidates this is where the realistic seat lives.",
    "Allotment letters, document verification, reporting to the college within the window — a missed reporting date is a lost seat, full stop.",
]))
c21.append(P("The free-exit and deposit rules from Chapter 8 apply: you may exit "
            "freely after Round 1, but leaving an allotted seat after Round 2 "
            "forfeits the deposit, and rules tighten further in Mop-Up. Decide your "
            "college hierarchy in advance, with your family and the fee ceilings "
            "from Chapter 8 — counselling season does not leave time for fresh "
            "financial deliberation."))
c21.append(P("Counselling for AYUSH, BDS and nursing courses runs on parallel "
            "committees and portals with their own schedules; if those courses are "
            "in your consideration set, follow their official notices separately."))
S += chapter(23, "After the Exam: Result to Allotment", c21)
S.append(PageBreak())

# ============================================================== CH 24 PARENTS (new)
cp = []
cp.append(P("This page is for the person often paying for the season and never "
             "given an instruction manual. The support a NEET aspirant needs is "
             "specific, cheap, and mostly about what not to do.", lead))
cp.append(bullets([
    "The calendar is public. The dates that matter to you: registration opens around February 2027 (the 2026 window ran 8 Feb to 8 Mar), the exam is expected on a Sunday in early May, and counselling runs July to September. Ask once a month: 'any official update?' — and trust only neet.nta.nic.in.",
    "The money conversation deserves one evening, early. Government-college MBBS fees are modest; private and deemed colleges run into lakhs per year. Set the ceiling before counselling, so a rank in May does not become a family crisis in July.",
    "Scam radar: anyone selling leaked papers, guaranteed seats or paid answer keys is committing a crime. In 2026, a real leak cancelled a national exam and buyers were the biggest losers. There are no shortcuts — only the official portal.",
    "Coaching is optional, not required. NCERT, previous papers and this handbook's calendar are the core; coaching adds structure. Judge spend against that honestly.",
    "Ask about the process, not the marks. 'What did the error log say this week?' builds a candidate; 'how much did you score?' builds an anxious one. The mock score is a moving average — treat it as data, and expect bad weeks in December and February.",
    "Feed the routine, not the pressure: a fixed study spot, phone-free blocks, dinner at a reliable hour, and sleep defended like tuition money.",
]))
cp.append(callout("THE ONE-SENTENCE VERSION",
                  "Your job this season is to keep the student's life steady and "
                  "the family's expectations honest — the syllabus is the "
                  "student's job, and 20 lakh of them manage it every year."))
S += chapter(24, "For Parents: The Support Playbook", cp)

# ============================================================== CH 25 (FAQ)
c22 = []
faq = [
    ("How many hours a day do I need?",
     "Class 12 students: 6 - 8 focused hours of self-study. Droppers: 8 - 10. Hours are the wrong metric anyway — a week with the error log used and the weekly review kept is a good week at any hour count."),
    ("Is NCERT enough for NEET?",
     "For Biology, close to entirely, with Exemplar for practice. For Chemistry, NCERT covers Inorganic and most theory; Physical and Organic need practice volumes beyond it. For Physics, NCERT gives the concepts and numericals practice must come from a standard objective series."),
    ("Can I prepare without coaching?",
     "Yes — the syllabus is public NCERT, PYQs are published, and mock series are available independently. Coaching provides structure and pace; self-study with this handbook's calendar, weekly chapter tests and an error log provides the same discipline."),
    ("When does registration for NEET 2027 open?",
     "Not yet notified. The 2026 window ran 8 February to 8 March 2026; a similar February 2027 window is expected. Set a reminder for the first week of February and watch neet.nta.nic.in only."),
    ("Will NEET 2027 be online?",
     "Unknown. 2026 was pen-and-paper; reports after the 2026 leak suggested computer-based testing was being considered, but nothing was notified as of September 2026. Prepare content-first; practise a few online mocks for safety."),
    ("How many attempts do I get?",
     "There is no attempt cap. The binding constraints are age (17 by 31 December of the admission year) and the Class 12 PCB percentage (50 / 40 / 45 by category)."),
    ("What score do I need for a government MBBS seat?",
     "It moves every year with the paper and the state. In 2026, 670+ competed for top colleges nationally; 620 - 670 was competitive in most states; reserved categories and state quotas shift these bands materially. Aim at a mock streak above your target, not at 'the cutoff'."),
    ("Biology or Physics — where should an average student invest?",
     "Biology first, always: it is half the paper and the cheapest marks in it. But do not abandon Physics — it is the rank-shifter precisely because half the field does."),
    ("What is the 1 - 7 - 30 rule?",
     "A revision cadence: engage a chapter on day 1, revise and re-solve it within 7 days, and test it again within 30 days. It is the cheapest memory insurance known."),
    ("Is a drop year worth it?",
     "Only with a diagnosis. If your score came from accuracy and pacing errors or a fixable content gap, a structured drop year has strong expected value. If it came from an unwillingness to study daily, a repeat year amplifies that, not the score."),
    ("Which language should I take the exam in?",
     "The one you think and study in. In 2026, 18 of 22.8 lakh candidates chose English and 3.45 lakh chose Hindi; translation quality is equal, comprehension is not."),
    ("What happens if a question is wrong on the paper?",
     "Per NTA's published rules: if no option is correct or the question is dropped, every candidate who appeared gets +4 for it — attempted or not. Multi-correct questions are handled the same generous way."),
    ("Do I need to register separately for state counselling?",
     "Yes. AIQ (MCC) and your state quota are separate registrations, fees, documents and timelines. Most serious candidates do both."),
    ("How early should I start mocks?",
     "Chapter tests from October; one full 180-minute mock a week from January; two to three a week in April. Analysed at 3:1 — three hours of analysis per hour of testing."),
    ("What if boards and NEET preparation clash in February?",
     "They are the same syllabus. Switch the format, not the content: written board practice daily, 30 - 40 NEET MCQs to stay sharp, one weekly mock. Resume full NEET mode the day boards end."),
    ("Can I use a calculator in the exam?",
     "No. None is permitted. Which is why mental arithmetic and clean algebra need daily practice from September, not April."),
    ("Are there seats outside MBBS worth planning for?",
     "Yes — BDS, BAMS, BHMS, BUMS, BSMS, BVSc and AH, and B.Sc. Nursing (including MNS via NEET). Decide your hierarchy before counselling, not during it."),
    ("How do I know my category certificate will be accepted?",
     "It must be in the prescribed format, from the competent authority, current for the admission year (OBC - NCL and EWS certificates have validity windows). Verify against the bulletin's annexures in advance."),
    ("What is the biggest scam risk this season?",
     "Paid 'leaked papers' and 'answer-key groups' on Telegram and WhatsApp. In 2026 a real leak cancelled a national exam; every buyer of such material was a loser. Official is official; everything else is a trap."),
    ("What single habit most improves a NEET score?",
     "The error log. Every wrong, guessed or slow question, bucketed and revisited weekly. It converts every mistake you will ever make into a question you will never lose again."),
]
c22.append(P("Straight answers to the questions aspirants and parents actually ask, "
             "in the order they usually ask them.", lead))
for q, a in faq:
    c22.append(KeepTogether([
        P(q, h2), P(a)]))
S += chapter(25, "Twenty Questions, Answered Straight", c22)
S.append(PageBreak())

# ============================================================== CH 23 checklist
c23 = []
c23.append(P("The whole season as tick-boxes. Print this page mentally; it is the "
             "handbook reduced to its verbs.", lead))
def check_block(title, items):
    rows = [[Paragraph("<b>%s</b>" % title, ParagraphStyle("cb", parent=cell,
             fontName="Helvetica-Bold", textColor=NAVY))]]
    for it in items:
        rows.append([Paragraph("[&nbsp;&nbsp;]&nbsp; " + it, cell)])
    t = Table(rows, colWidths=[DOC_W])
    t.setStyle(TableStyle([
        ("BACKGROUND", (0, 0), (0, 0), CREAM2),
        ("VALIGN", (0, 0), (-1, -1), "TOP"),
        ("BOX", (0, 0), (-1, -1), 0.5, LINE),
        ("LINEBELOW", (0, 0), (0, 0), 1, GOLD),
        ("TOPPADDING", (0, 0), (-1, -1), 4),
        ("BOTTOMPADDING", (0, 0), (-1, -1), 4),
        ("LEFTPADDING", (0, 0), (-1, -1), 8)]))
    return t
c23.append(check_block("SEPTEMBER - OCTOBER 2026", [
    "Weekly rotation across all three subjects begins; error log opens today",
    "Diagnostics done: one chapter test per subject to map the starting line",
    "Books finalised: NCERT + Exemplar + PYQs + one practice layer; nothing more bought",
    "Daily numericals (Physics) and daily NCERT recall (Biology) habits running"]))
c23.append(Spacer(1, 6))
c23.append(check_block("NOVEMBER - DECEMBER 2026", [
    "First pass of the full syllabus completed by 31 December",
    "Weekly chapter tests and the Sunday 30-minute review held every week",
    "Exceptions notebook (Biology + Inorganic) one-third filled and revised weekly",
    "Category certificate (if claiming one) verified as valid for the admission year"]))
c23.append(check_block("JANUARY - FEBRUARY 2027", [
    "Full-syllabus learning closed; timed subject-wise tests begin",
    "One full 180-minute mock per week at 2 PM, analysed at 3:1",
    "First week of February: registration window checked on neet.nta.nic.in",
    "Form submitted by week one of the window, not the last day; correction window used if needed"]))
c23.append(check_block("MARCH - APRIL 2027", [
    "Board written practice daily; 30 - 40 MCQs never dropped",
    "April: two to three full mocks a week; error-log raids on top ten weak chapters",
    "Exam-day order of sections frozen; admit card downloaded and verified",
    "Travel and stay for the allotted city arranged in advance"]))
c23.append(check_block("EXAM WEEK AND AFTER", [
    "Sleep protected; nothing new learned; formulas and diagrams revised lightly",
    "One mock or sectional at the real 2 PM slot early in the week",
    "Answer key and recorded responses checked; challenges filed within the window",
    "MCC and state portals both registered on; choice list decided with the family fee ceiling"]))
c23.append(Spacer(1, 8))
c23.append(Paragraph("Eight months is a long time. It is exactly long enough.", quote))
S += chapter(26, "The Master Checklist", c23)

